	<p>Intended reporting process:</p>
	<ol>
		<li>The accessor create the report, add the assessements general information and log its assessement for each Success Criterion results.</li>
		<li>A reviewer re-open the assement, self-indentify in the review section, review the original assesment and put any remark along with the review. Once the review completed, the reviewer will create as many work items as needed. This step can be repeated as needed but when there is more than 3 reviews you should consider to produce a new ACR and start over this process.</li>
		<li>Closing - A contributor submit a change to make the assesemen no longer valid or being superseeded by another ACR</li>
	</ol>
</details>
